WEBVTT

00:02:00.015 --> 00:02:02.046
LO: and so I've showed up as a potato

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:06.416
to some meetings for friends
at other organizations

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:07.761
and things like that.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:12.245
AG: The coronavirus pandemic has thrown
many of us into the deep end

00:02:12.269 --> 00:02:13.646
of working remotely.

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:16.196
While some people have found
creative ways to swim,

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:18.898
many others are struggling
just to stay afloat.

00:02:19.636 --> 00:02:22.986
The good news is that remote work
is not uncharted waters.

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:26.466
We've actually been doing it
and studying it for a long time,

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.056
and with those lessons in hand,

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:30.496
you might actually be
more prepared than you think